{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-17T10:05:58.060Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Both verifies pass:\n- Task verify `node --import tsx --import ./tests/git-test-env.ts --test tests/autopilot-step.test.ts`: 21/21 pass.\n- Proposal verify `pnpm verify`: EXIT=0 (typechecks, build, all 230+ CLI/UI tests, lint).\n\nSummary of what I built:\n\n**`src/core/status/autopilot-marker.ts`** — reads, writes and updates a change folder's `.run/autopilot.md`; frontmatter is `item`, `queue_approval`, `created_at`, then `planner_started_at` and `approved_at`. Missing/unparsable reads as none.\n\n**`src/core/status/autopilot-view.ts`** — `readAutopilotView` reads from files only: queue existence/parse error, active usage-limit pause, active approved change ids, and the first non-landed queue row with its item, row, approval, and (for an active/archived change) id, folder, approved flag, marker, `currentPlanRun` and `readNextStep`.\n\n**`src/core/status/autopilot-step.ts`** — pure `autopilotStep(view)` that checks the spec table's rows in order and returns `done`/`wait`/`plan-next`/`plan`/`approve`/`land`/`stop`, with stop reasons and the resuming command.\n\n**`tests/autopilot-step.test.ts`** — one test per table row in order against hand-built views, with queue/approval/ready-plan-run rows read from temporary projects without git, plus the marker round trip.\n\nTwo disclosures are recorded in the result file: the `scenario()` helper cannot look up status-inspection scenarios because the living spec has a duplicate scenario name (`Outside scope`), so the test transcribes the table into plain `node:test` rows as tasks 1 and 2 did (`Deviated`)."}}
